The app is built in `src/` (entry `src/App.tsx`, with `boardMachine.ts`, `archiveMachine.ts`, `appMachine.ts`, `calls.ts`, `types.ts`, `BoardPage.tsx`, `ArchivePage.tsx`). `./check` is clean and all 26 visible tests pass; I used 7 of the 15 check/test runs. I was unsure about a few choices the brief leaves open: add-card and add-item are disabled until their list has loaded, a move into a column that is still loading or failed is hidden, re-clicking the selected card reloads its checklist, and the one 404 console error in the tests is probably a favicon request (the app loads no resources). I also guarded against StrictMode dev restarts resending a write, which I reasoned through from the XState source but did not test in a dev build.